  "final_message": "I wrote `answer.json` from reading the code. I didn't run a simulation or the tests.\n\n```json\n{\"total_charge_attempts\": 4, \"last_attempt_day\": 7, \"final_subscription_status\": \"unpaid\", \"final_invoice_status\": \"open\"}\n```\n\n- **Attempts:** The first charge happens at subscribe, on day 0. The default policy (`DEFAULT_POLICY` in `billing/dunning.py`) then retries at days 1, 3 and 7 after the invoice was finalized. That makes four attempts in total.\n- **Last attempt:** Retries are counted from finalization, not from the previous attempt, so the last one is on day 7. The daily cycle picks up each retry as soon as it is due.\n- **Subscription:** The first failure moves it to `past_due`. When the fourth attempt fails, the retries have run out. The default final action is `mark_unpaid`, which moves the subscription to `unpaid`.\n- **Invoice:** Only the `cancel` final action marks the invoice uncollectible. The default leaves it `open`.\n\nI assumed the billing period is longer than 7 days, so no renewal invoice interferes. I didn't check the period length.",
